  promptText: Industrial trawlers have begun bottom-dragging in nearshore waters,
    degrading reef habitat and reducing fish stocks. Mobilising the village could
    expel fleets but risks violent confrontation.
  leftAnswer: Organised defence can halt damage and protect future food security.
  rightAnswer: Avoiding confrontation keeps families safe today while you seek alternatives.
